Lab Material
Lab 18: Integrate Ansible for Configuration Management in OpenStack
Objectives
Automate configuration management of OpenStack instances using Ansible
Implement automated patching and updates for OpenStack services
Deploy applications and configure instances using Ansible playbooks
Prerequisites
OpenStack environment with admin credentials
Minimum 2 Linux instances (Ubuntu 22.04/CentOS 8) in OpenStack
SSH access to instances
Python 3.8+ installed on control node
Basic understanding of YAML syntax
Setup Requirements
Control node (Ansible host) with:
2 vCPUs, 4GB RAM, 20GB storage
Target nodes (OpenStack instances):
1 for OpenStack services (controller)
1 for application deployment (compute)
Task 1: Set Up Ansible for OpenStack Configuration
1.1 Install Ansible on Control Node
sudo apt update
sudo apt install -y ansible python3-pip
pip3 install openstacksdk
Verification:

ansible --version
Expected Output:

ansible [core 2.12.0]
1.2 Configure Ansible Inventory
Create /etc/ansible/hosts:

[openstack_services]
controller ansible_host=192.168.1.10

[application_nodes]
compute1 ansible_host=192.168.1.20

[all:vars]
ansible_python_interpreter=/usr/bin/python3
ansible_user=ubuntu
ansible_ssh_private_key_file=~/.ssh/openstack_key.pem
Troubleshooting Tip:
If SSH connection fails, verify:

Key permissions (chmod 600 ~/.ssh/openstack_key.pem)
Security group rules in OpenStack
Task 2: Automate Patching and Updates
2.1 Create Patching Playbook
Create patch_update.yml: `yaml
name: Update OpenStack services hosts: openstack_services become: yes tasks:
name: Update all packages apt: update_cache: yes upgrade: dist when: ansible_os_family == 'Debian'

name: Reboot if required reboot: msg: "Reboot initiated by Ansible" connect_timeout: 5 reboot_timeout: 600 pre_reboot_delay: 0 post_reboot_delay: 30


### **2.2 Execute Playbook**
```bash
ansible-playbook patch_update.yml
Expected Outcome:
All packages updated on controller node with automatic reboot if kernel updated

Task 3: Instance Setup & Application Deployment
3.1 Create Instance Configuration Playbook
Create instance_setup.yml: `yaml
name: Configure application node hosts: application_nodes become: yes vars: app_user: demoapp tasks:
name: Create application user user: name: "{{ app_user }}" groups: sudo append: yes

name: Install Nginx apt: name: nginx state: present when: ansible_os_family == 'Debian'

name: Start Nginx service service: name: nginx state: started enabled: yes


### **3.2 Deploy Sample Application**
Add to `instance_setup.yml`:
```yaml
    - name: Deploy sample index.html
      copy:
        content: "<h1>Ansible-Managed OpenStack App</h1>"
        dest: /var/www/html/index.html
        owner: "{{ app_user }}"
        mode: '0644'
3.3 Run Deployment
ansible-playbook instance_setup.yml
Verification:

curl http://<compute_node_ip>
Expected Output:
<h1>Ansible-Managed OpenStack App</h1>

